### FamKit API — requires REST Client extension.
### baseUrl comes from your VS Code user settings (rest-client.environmentVariables.$shared.baseUrl).
### Run `func start` in src/famkit.Api and `npx azurite` first. Click "Send Request" above each block.

### 1. Pantry — should start empty
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry

### 2. Pantry — add an item
# @name addEggs
POST {{baseUrl}}/pantry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "eggs",
  "category": "fridge",
  "quantity": "1 dozen"
}

### 3. Pantry — add another item
# @name addFlour
POST {{baseUrl}}/pantry
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "flour",
  "category": "pantry"
}

### 4. Pantry — list again, should show both items
GET {{baseUrl}}/pantry

### 5. Pantry — delete the eggs item (uses the id from request #2's response)
@eggsId = {{addEggs.response.body.$.rowKey}}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/pantry/{{eggsId}}

### 6. Recipes — should start empty
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipes

### 7. Recipes — add a recipe
# @name addPancakes
POST {{baseUrl}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Pancakes",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "flour" },
    { "name": "milk" },
    { "name": "eggs" }
  ],
  "instructions": "Mix and cook."
}

### 8. Recipes — evaluate by recipe id (uses the id from request #7's response)
@pancakesId = {{addPancakes.response.body.$.id}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/recipes/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipeId": "{{pancakesId}}"
}

### 9. Recipes — evaluate inline ingredients, no saved recipe needed
POST {{baseUrl}}/recipes/evaluate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "flour" },
    { "name": "sugar" }
  ]
}

### 10. Recipes — delete the pancakes recipe
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/recipes/{{pancakesId}}

### 11. Meal plan — suggest recipes from current pantry (needs Spoonacular:ApiKey set + non-empty pantry)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mealplan/suggest

### 12. Vision — identify ingredients from a photo (raw body, Content-Type must match the file)
### Replace the path below with a real image on your machine.
POST {{baseUrl}}/vision/identify
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< C:\temp\pantry.jpg
